What the nethack wiki says seems to match much better with my own
experience; he re-appears every 50-249 turns with a chance of 1/6.
While this may happen - assuming a linear function - *on average*
every ~900 turns, it may as well happen every 50 turns, and even
Double Trouble. Or this re-appearance may, in other cases, happen
not even once (besides his guaranteed appearances). The _average_
that you presume is only significant if your number of samples is
large! A dozen (or less) re-appearance events is far too small to
say anything.

Besides that, just to let you know, those numbers that I posted
were all based on games where I typically teleport (if possible)
across levels. But you can never know how long you will have to
stay in Gehennom. In one game the stairs on non-teleport levels
are close, while in other games you have to pass the whole level.
In one game (even as chaotic) you are thrown again and again back
by the Force, while in other games (even as lawful) you are lucky.
In one game you will trigger that 1/6 probability every time, in
other games never. So all your suggestions, while valid, are not
the least any guarantee to not meet the Wizard half a dozen times
(or even more often) on a regular basis.

